## Owner flags

1. **The road meet's day (calendar conflict, resolved on the page — please confirm).** The closed M3 page (ch16, day 45: "I've got eighteen days to the road meet") and its ledger put the meet on **day 63**. The M4 packet enters "twelve days after the preliminary ruling" (day 66) with the meet still "close", and BOOK_MAP §3 orders the small room (item 9) **before** Silver Season (item 10) — so day 63 cannot stand without breaking either the packet's entry or the spine's order. Resolution on the page: the confluence's stewards **put the meet back eight days "for repairs to the hall"** (ch21 Lira's card, re-chalked; ch21 the north wall; ch23 Rooke walks the floor slower; ch24 Rooke's *Mine*). The repair is the false quarter's origin (the river under the great doors lifted the south-west planks). M3's page stays true as written. Alternative if declined: move the small room to before day 63 and drop "twelve days".
2. **The escort order's count and address (#44).** The Tier B body is 75 words and carries no name ("the enrollee of record therein named"). To honour #44 (*Caelen Hesk-ward* in instruments) without touching protected text, the order is read with a six-word heading, *In the matter of Caelen Hesk-ward.*, and Cael counts **eighty-one** "from the name to the hand". If the owner prefers the name inside the body (as M1's first page), the count needs re-squaring.
3. **The hearing provision (M8 hook).** Two paragraphs; para 2 lets the advocate of record be heard at the close by the seat's leave (no recorded use). This is the BOOK_MAP §11 #4 default's "fossil provision", set up lightly and kept unmentioned at the seat. Karis is entered in the door log as *Advocate of record for the respondent, under the hearing provision* — please confirm before M7–M8 rely on it.
4. **Seln's window** carries his trade's counts (nineteen postings; sixty-three subjects; the fourth posting twelve years ago; the green corridor) and his own reports as "true among true things" in the same drawer as Cael's receipts. No Shadow, no sealed thing, no content of the records, no *falsification*. Check the plant's altitude before M6.
5. **Lira's carters** are a Lira cutaway; one is a woman (unnamed) — the packet left their sex open. The last Arbiter station is described (low stone, frame-house behind, sigil over the door) and placed past the last chartered waystation; check against M9's road.
