**30,437 against the asked ~32,700** (−2.3k). The whole redrafts came out tighter (ch22 4,790 → 4,089; ch27 5,338 → 4,962), and P2.2/P2.3 removed duplication by instruction (ch23 4,322 → 3,833). I added back only beats with a job: Lira's "Forty days from what?" and her chalk; Withrow commending the lodge-man's board; Bracken reading his letter to the district seat; Brom's one-step test in the Crown yard; Seln's nineteen boxes and his hand on the shelf; the Current girl in Lira's window; Ephram's grievance line. I declined to make up the rest, because the remaining room would have been restatement of exactly what the cold read asked me to cut.

